From a423b46bac557c5f08a187ddd6dbe9dd13ea77b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <noreply@invalid>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:03:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 73/81] vulkan/wsi: Horizon, the swapchain decision is logged
 against the device

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 4 (Horizon WSI backend)
Why: the four INFO messages that report the present path and the
 registered layout named the swapchain as their object, and all four run
 inside wsi_horizon_surface_create_swapchain - before wsi_common.c calls
 wsi_swapchain_to_handle, which is what sets
 vk_object_base::client_visible. vk_log.c answers an object that is not
 yet visible with
   MESA: warning: vk_log*() called with client-invisible object 0x...
         of type VK_OBJECT_TYPE_SWAPCHAIN_KHR
 and emits it above its own !MESA_DEBUG early-out, so the warning
 appears in every build whether or not a messenger is installed to
 receive the message that provoked it. The backend was making Mesa warn
 about the backend's own diagnostics, once per line.
Evidence: docs/hw-logs/t_vk_wsi_mt-run20-review-fixes-PASS.log contains
 188 lines matching "vk_log*() called with client-invisible object",
 against 52 checks. Cross build only for the fix itself:
 aarch64-none-elf-gcc from ghcr.io/d3fau4/nx-dev with meson's own
 command line for this file and -fsyntax-only, no diagnostics. NOT
 verified on hardware; the count above is the measurement this patch
 predicts will become zero.
Upstream: no - this file is the Horizon backend itself.

The VkDevice is already a parameter of this function, is client-visible
for the whole of it, and is the object the messages are really about:
they describe a decision the device has just made about a swapchain that
does not exist as a handle yet.

Deliberately still vk_logi and not mesa_logi. These go out through the
debug-utils messenger because Phase 6's fourth exit criterion asks for
the zero-copy decision to be observable by an application at run time,
and mesa_log* is not observable that way - it goes to the log and
nowhere else. tests/t_vk_wsi_mt.c reads the decision back through the
messenger to check which present path it got, so moving them would have
silently disabled that check rather than breaking it.

VK_FROM_HANDLE is declared with the function's other locals rather than
at the `done:` label that uses it, because a label must be followed by a
statement and that macro expands to a declaration.

The vk_logw in wsi_horizon_present_zero_copy keeps naming the swapchain:
by present time the handle exists and the object is visible, which is
the case this warning is meant to distinguish.

Found in review of PR #9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011kZa1YF3mTLVEZrLyzgsVr
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
index 2c033e9..2f41ef6 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_horizon.c
@@ -2022,6 +2022,12 @@ wsi_horizon_surface_create_swapchain(VkIcdSurfaceBase *icd_surface,
    struct wsi_horizon_surface *surface = wsi_horizon_surface(icd_surface);
    VkResult result;
 
+   /* Declared here rather than at the `done:` label that uses it: a
+    * label must be followed by a statement, and VK_FROM_HANDLE expands
+    * to a declaration. See that label for why the device and not the
+    * swapchain is what these messages name. */
+   VK_FROM_HANDLE(vk_device, log_device, device);
+
    assert(pCreateInfo->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_INFO_KHR);
 
    /* THE FORMAT IS RE-VALIDATED HERE, not only offered by get_formats.
@@ -2246,13 +2252,31 @@ done:
    /* The decision, its reason, and enough of the geometry to check it
     * against — at INFO through the debug-utils messenger, so an
     * application can observe which path it got instead of reading a log
-    * afterwards. */
-   vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&chain->base.base),
+    * afterwards.
+    *
+    * REPORTED AGAINST THE DEVICE, NOT THE SWAPCHAIN, and that is not a
+    * cosmetic choice. Every one of these runs before wsi_common.c turns
+    * `chain` into a VkSwapchainKHR, and vk_object_base::client_visible
+    * is set by the *_to_handle() that has not happened yet. vk_log.c
+    * answers a not-yet-visible object with
+    *   MESA: warning: vk_log*() called with client-invisible object
+    *         0x... of type VK_OBJECT_TYPE_SWAPCHAIN_KHR
+    * and it does so above its own !MESA_DEBUG early-out, so the warning
+    * is emitted in every build whether or not anybody is listening to
+    * the INFO message that caused it. Run 20's log carries 188 of them.
+    *
+    * The VkDevice is client-visible and is the object these messages
+    * are really about anyway — they describe a decision the device just
+    * made. Keeping them on vk_log rather than moving them to mesa_logi
+    * is deliberate: the debug-utils messenger is how an application
+    * observes the present path, which is the whole reason Phase 6 asked
+    * for the decision to be observable at run time. */
+   vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&log_device->base),
            "wsi_horizon: %s (%u images, %ux%u, swap interval %u)",
            chain->decision, image_count, extent.width, extent.height,
            chain->swap_interval);
    if (!chain->zero_copy && why != NULL) {
-      vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&chain->base.base),
+      vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&log_device->base),
               "wsi_horizon: zero-copy was declined because %s", why);
    }
 
@@ -2274,7 +2298,7 @@ done:
     */
    if (chain->zero_copy) {
       const struct wsi_horizon_image_info *i0 = &chain->images[0].info;
-      vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&chain->base.base),
+      vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&log_device->base),
               "wsi_horizon: layout: stride %" PRIu32 " B (%" PRIu32 " px), "
               "block height %u GOBs (log2 %" PRIu32 ", %u rows), kind 0x%02x, "
               "%sblock-linear, display GOB order %s, offset %" PRIu64 " B, "
@@ -2292,7 +2316,7 @@ done:
              ii->block_height_log2 != i0->block_height_log2 ||
              ii->pte_kind != i0->pte_kind || ii->size_B != i0->size_B ||
              ii->offset_B != i0->offset_B) {
-            vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&chain->base.base),
+            vk_logi(VK_LOG_OBJS(&log_device->base),
                     "wsi_horizon: layout: image %" PRIu32 " differs: stride %"
                     PRIu32 " B, block height log2 %" PRIu32 ", kind 0x%02x, "
                     "offset %" PRIu64 " B, allocation %" PRIu64 " B",
